            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous rupture of renal angiomyolipoma presenting as acute abdomen.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>148-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Five cases of renal angiomyolipoma which underwent spontaneous rupture are described. These patients presented as an &quot;acute abdomen&quot; for which the diagnosis was not initially apparent. A high index of suspicion is required to make the diagnosis even with modern imaging techniques. The treatment of these tumours is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
